Hint:\(E=\dfrac{kq}{r^2}\)

Step:Find the magnitude of the electric field at point\(O\).
The electric field due to point charge is given by;
\(E=\dfrac{kq}{r^2}\)along radially outwards
The electric field due to point charge at point\(A\) is given by;
\(E_A=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(OA\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(H\) is given by;
\(E_H=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(OH\)
Both\(E_A ~\text{and}~E_H\)are equal in magnitude and opposite in direction so,
they will cancel each other.
The electric field due to point charge at point\(B\) is given by;
\(E_B=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(BO\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(G\) is given by;
\(E_G=\dfrac{k(2q)}{l^2}\)along\(GO\)
Both\(E_G ~\text{and}~E_B\)are in opposite in direction so net electric field
due to\(E_G ~\text{and}~E_B\)will be given by;
\(E_{net}=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(GO\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(D\) is given by;
\(E_D=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(DO\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(E\) is given by;
\(E_E=\dfrac{k(2q)}{l^2}\)along\(EO\)
Both\(E_D ~\text{and}~E_E\)are in opposite in direction so net electric field
due to\(E_D ~\text{and}~E_E\)will be given by;
\(E_{net}=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(EO\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(F\) is given by;
\(E_F=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(FO\)
The electric field due to point charge at point\(C\) is given by;
\(E_C=\dfrac{k(2q)}{l^2}\)along\(CO\)
Both\(E_F ~\text{and}~E_C\)are in opposite in direction so net electric field
due to\(E_F ~\text{and}~E_C\)will be given by;
\(E_{net}=\dfrac{kq}{l^2}\)along\(CO\)
Therefore, the net contribution of the electric field due to\(E_G
~\text{and}~E_B\),\(E_D ~\text{and}~E_E\)and\(E_F ~\text{and}~E_C\)are given by;
\(E_{net}=\dfrac{1}{4\pi\varepsilon_0}\dfrac{q}{(2l^2)}(2\sqrt{2}-1)\)
Hence, option (1) is the correct answer.<div style="margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;"><div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style="padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.15); color:#16a34a;">🟢 Easy · 74% Got This Correct</span></div><div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;"><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;"><div style="color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;">(1) ✓</div><div style="font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;">74%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(2)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">8%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(3)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">11%</div></div><div style="padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);"><div>(4)</div><div style="font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;">10%</div></div></div></div>

